{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>But his bow remained taut.</b> Indeed, Joseph's bow — to shoot an arrow against slanderers — remained taut in strength, namely the king, as he said to his servants: הֲנִמְצָא כָזֶה אִישׁ אֲשֶׁר רוּחַ אֱלֹהִים בּוֹ (Genesis 41:38), and in his saying: אֵין נָבוֹן וְחָכָם כָּמוֹךָ (Genesis 41:39)." "<b>And the arms of his hands were made supple.</b> By Pharaoh's placing his ring on his hand." "<b>From the hands of the Mighty One of Jacob.</b> Indeed, this deliverance and success came to you from the hands of Jacob's Mighty One, who sustains his sons among the nations so as to preserve them at the end of them all — in accordance with the meaning of the name Jacob, which indicates that he remains in the wake and at the end of all the nations. And so He established you and delivered you from the wielders of arrows who hated you and embittered and strove against you." "<b>From there.</b> And from the way of this goodness of His." "<b>The Shepherd, the Stone of Israel.</b> He is the shepherd of Israel, who endure among the nations like a precious stone or an ordinary stone that endures for a long time — as in the matter of הִתְגַּזֶּרֶת אֶבֶן דִּי לָא בִידַיִן וּמְחַת לְצַלְמָא עַל רַגְלוֹהִי (Daniel 2:34). And they are Israel, for they strive with Elohim and with men — as the Sages said: in every place they went, they became princes to their masters."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:29.843551799Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}